1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,002
RTLRefine: check an AI repair and keep executable regressions.
Model results are actual recorded runs; the native checks below execute fresh.

2
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:15,101
This historical UART pair passes its closed-loop smoke test.
A matching transmitter and receiver can conceal the same wrong bit order.

3
00:00:15,790 --> 00:00:22,791
The supplied independent serial-peer test rejects it. No checked export.
Expected data comes from offered bytes, not corrected reference RTL.

4
00:00:22,865 --> 00:00:33,868
Actual bit-center samples: 0x01 becomes 0x80 on the original wire.
The original receiver reverses bytes too. The selected repair corrects both.

5
00:00:34,059 --> 00:00:44,065
Actual recorded Nemotron response on Nebius Token Factory.
Six development requests are retained; the final two-request run passed.

6
00:00:44,284 --> 00:00:49,288
The agent changes the real vendor RX file. Headers and ports stay fixed.
All earlier wrong, uncompilable and truncated responses remain in the evidence.

7
00:00:49,314 --> 00:00:54,317
Its selected TX edit corrects serialization too. Both leaves are rebuilt independently
inside the read-only adapter; no corrected implementation is the test oracle.

8
00:01:00,047 --> 00:01:09,055
Fresh verification: eight fixed profiles and the exact standalone CI runner pass.
5-8 data bits, serial frames, resets, backpressure and overrun: 186,772 evaluations.

9
00:01:15,924 --> 00:01:25,931
The downloaded checker runs on checked source, both original files, then restored source.
Exit codes 0, 1, 0: a returning defect fails the same unchanged tests.

10
00:01:31,746 --> 00:01:39,749
Reopen the same three-file UART project through the general ZIP workspace.
Its protected tests and reusable CI remain attached; no model key is needed.

11
00:01:39,906 --> 00:01:47,912
Commit the included workflow to recheck pushes and pull requests.
JSON and JUnit reports distinguish pass, design regression and setup failure.

12
00:01:51,095 --> 00:02:01,098
For the separate supported FIFO contract, symbolic checks find a missed case.
This authored fixture passes smoke tests; its failure is replayed against a Python queue.

13
00:02:01,652 --> 00:02:09,655
This earlier actual NVIDIA FIFO repair is explicitly recorded.
Final bounded checks and portable regressions accompany its selected source.

14
00:02:09,655 --> 00:02:17,658
Known external UART development and authored bounded FIFO examples; no unseen accuracy
or physical timing/CDC claim. Source and test build: github.com/ehdtjq08/RTLRefine
